<title>CANADA: CWB details primary elevator space, railcar unload.</title>
<headline>CWB details primary elevator space, railcar unload.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vacant space in country elevators across the Prairies held at 20 percent for the second consecutive week, Canadian Wheat Board said.</p>
<p>Primary elevator space in Manitoba and Saskatchewan averaged 18 percent while Alberta vacancy stood at 25 percent for an overall average of 20 percent, CWB said.</p>
<p>Hopper car unloads in Vancouver for the week ended Oct 27 totaled 2,911 below the 3,400 target, Prince Rupert unloads were 1,260 compared to the 1,500 target, Thunder Bay was 2,987 versus the 3,000 target and Churchill unloads were 472 compared to the 300 hopper car target.</p>
<p>--Gilbert Le Gras 204-947-3548</p>
